    "references": [
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 10.20.090 block 0",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 0,
          "component_id": "88012093-06de-561e-936a-918d7b72dec3",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 294,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:10.20.090:block:0",
          "start": 0
        },
        "quote": "(a) Prohibition. No person operating or occupying a motor vehicle on a street, highway, alley, parking lot or driveway shall operate or permit the operation of any sound amplification system from within the vehicle so that the sound is audible at a distance of 50 or more feet from the vehicle.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:10.20.090:block:0#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 10.20.090 block 1",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 1,
          "component_id": "80c6c6ad-616b-5213-93ac-73692ec2ef5d",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 344,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:10.20.090:block:1",
          "start": 295
        },
        "quote": "(b) Definitions. For the purpose of this section:",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:10.20.090:block:1#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 10.20.090 block 2",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 2,
          "component_id": "96037ed0-c323-5117-8658-8b7c3ab7645d",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 768,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:10.20.090:block:2",
          "start": 345
        },
        "quote": "“Audible” means any sound produced by a sound amplification system from within a vehicle which can be heard at a distance of 50 feet or more. Measurement standards shall be by the auditory senses, based upon direct line of sight. Words or phrases need not be discernible and bass reverberations are included. The motor vehicle may be stopped, standing, parked or moving on a street, highway, alley, parking lot or driveway.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:10.20.090:block:2#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 10.20.090 block 3",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 3,
          "component_id": "0e959af3-ece9-5af1-9d16-d354005fc9bf",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 925,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:10.20.090:block:3",
          "start": 769
        },
        "quote": "“Sound amplification system” means any radio, tape player, compact disc player, loudspeaker, or other electronic device used for the amplification of sound.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:10.20.090:block:3#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 10.20.090 block 4",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 4,
          "component_id": "ed48ac4f-b86c-58ad-9f27-ed383d803cde",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 1166,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:10.20.090:block:4",
          "start": 926
        },
        "quote": "(c) Defense to Prosecution. It is an affirmative defense to a charge under this section that the operator of the vehicle was not otherwise prohibited by law from operating the sound amplification system, and that any of the following apply:",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:10.20.090:block:4#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 10.20.090 block 5",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 5,
          "component_id": "cb68e400-8d4e-54d6-81e8-f57a22771f2a",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 1285,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:10.20.090:block:5",
          "start": 1167
        },
        "quote": "(1) The system was being operated to request medical or vehicular assistance or to warn of a hazardous road condition;",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:10.20.090:block:5#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 10.20.090 block 6",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 6,
          "component_id": "b1b8971c-74ef-5c59-93af-6b21464e841f",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 1344,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:10.20.090:block:6",
          "start": 1286
        },
        "quote": "(2) The vehicle was an emergency or public safety vehicle;",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:10.20.090:block:6#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 10.20.090 block 7",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 7,
          "component_id": "53fdb2c6-5aef-514a-9b5e-8f9195160b51",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 1449,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:10.20.090:block:7",
          "start": 1345
        },
        "quote": "(3) The vehicle was owned and operated by the City or a gas, electric, communications or refuse company;",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:10.20.090:block:7#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 10.20.090 block 8",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 8,
          "component_id": "78815a76-c9e2-5f9f-b451-ca26b283def1",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 1660,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:10.20.090:block:8",
          "start": 1450
        },
        "quote": "(4) The system was used for the purpose of giving instructions, directions, talks, addresses, lectures or transmitting music to any persons or assemblage of persons in compliance with ordinances of the City; or",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:10.20.090:block:8#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 10.20.090 block 9",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 9,
          "component_id": "9a0740b9-a049-523d-85e0-a2c5b1950ac3",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 1893,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:10.20.090:block:9",
          "start": 1661
        },
        "quote": "(5) The vehicle was used in authorized public activities, such as parades, fireworks, sporting events, musical productions and other activities which have the approval of the department of the City authorized to grant such approval.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:10.20.090:block:9#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 10.20.090 block 10",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 10,
          "component_id": "2802e314-d896-5738-8f4e-10eb58debabe",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 2078,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:10.20.090:block:10",
          "start": 1894
        },
        "quote": "(d) Penalty. Any person who violates any of the provisions of this section is guilty of an ordinance violation and, upon conviction, shall be punished in accordance with TMC 1.10.070 .",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:10.20.090:block:10#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 10.20.090 block 11",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 11,
          "component_id": "44131e47-9975-53f4-aff3-09661cec426d",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 2435,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:10.20.090:block:11",
          "start": 2079
        },
        "quote": "(e) Penalty – Subsequent Violations. Upon a second or subsequent offense committed within six months after the previous offense, upon conviction thereof, a fine of at least $250.00 shall be imposed. The court may impose a lesser fine if the person establishes that the sound amplification system has been removed from the vehicle. (Ord. 19966 § 1, 9-1-15.)",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:10.20.090:block:11#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
